-- The latest versions' notes, for the "What's new" window (Map/News.lua), from CHANGELOG.md.
-- Generated by tools/changelog/build.py; regenerate rather than edit.

local _, ns = ...

ns.MapChangelog = {
	{ version = "Unreleased", date = "", heads = { [1] = "Improved", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aOpenMap has its own icon|r, a compass over a parchment map, in the AddOns list, on the minimap button and in the map's menu (it borrowed the game's Eastern Kingdoms icon).",
		"|cff6e2c0aOpenMap is back on GitHub|r, at github.com/openmap-world/openmap: Report a problem opens a report there again, and What's new and the AddOns list link to it.",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.7.1-beta", date = "2026-10-21", heads = { [1] = "Fixed", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aThe map loads the zone you pan or zoom to again|r: with an addon adding map icons, it could stay on the zone you started on, so the zone you'd panned to showed none of their icons until you clicked it. Its setting, once Follow the view, is now |cff6e2c0aLoad the zone in view|r.",
		"|cff6e2c0aFlight masters you've learned are in colour|r, all of them: OpenMap knew only the ones it had seen you visit since it was installed (and, on a client not in English, none). It now asks the game which you've found.",
		"|cff6e2c0aRetail: your arrow and the map's icons where they are in the cities|r: in Stormwind, your arrow, Blizzard's flight master and the other icons on the city's map were drawn tens of yards from where they are (a player's report).",
		"|cff6e2c0aWith Enhance QoL|r, OpenMap says once in chat to turn off its Mover > World Map: the two both size the map, and its scale goes wrong (a player's finding).",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.7.0-beta", date = "2026-10-20", heads = { [1] = "New", [2] = "Improved", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aOpenMap for retail|r (Midnight): the same seamless map, from retail's own maps. Every continent on Azeroth's map, its zones stitched in as you zoom with their explored areas painted (or hidden until you've been there, as Blizzard's own map does), Blizzard's art as it is; the world's parchment out to its torn edge and on past it; dungeon and raid entrances from the encounter journal with every floor of their maps, flight masters, boats and zeppelins, the close-up minimap. A download of its own on CurseForge.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe map stays open while you talk to an NPC|r (or open a vendor, the bags' windows ...): the windowed map is no longer put away to make room. Escape still closes it; maximized, it behaves as before.",
		"|cff6e2c0aReopen map: Center on player, keep zoom|r (the menu's Reopen map, and Options): the map opens on you at the zoom you closed it at.",
		"|cff6e2c0aChoose your map|r: the choice the first time the map opens is in the map window's own frame, with plainer words.",
		"|cff6e2c0aA little lighter at the whole-world view|r: a city's map isn't drawn at all until it starts to fade in (before, it was drawn unseen).",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.5.0-beta", date = "2026-10-16", heads = { [1] = "New", [12] = "Improved", [18] = "Fixed", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aKhaz Modan's blank land painted|r: the stretches between Dun Morogh, Wetlands, Loch Modan, Searing Gorge and the Badlands that no zone map covers, and the coast round them, painted by hand by Santiago Reyes in the zone maps' own style, from Blizzard's art and following the game's terrain (used with his permission). The first of the gaps between zones to be filled; Options' |cff6e2c0aFilled gaps|r turns them off.",
		"|cff6e2c0aMaps of City of Dalaran and Excavation Site: Wetlands|r, drawn by Santiago Reyes and used with his permission: click their entrances in Alterac Mountains and the Wetlands (they opened on a blank page before). \"Map by Santiago Reyes\" at their foot, as with his others.",
		"|cff6e2c0aAirships to Zephras Isle|r: the flying boats at the Dalaran skydock (Alterac Mountains) and in Mulgore are on the map; click one and Zephras Isle's map opens in the window, as a dungeon's does, and Back takes you to the world where you were. (Under the Boats switch.)",
		"|cff6e2c0aMaps of Ruins of Lordaeron and The Hall of Thanes|r, two of WoW Forever's own dungeons, which the game has no map of: drawn by Santiago Reyes and used with his permission. Click their entrances in Undercity and Ironforge; the map shows \"Map by Santiago Reyes\" at its foot.",
		"|cff6e2c0aDungeon Journal|r: with Exehn's Dungeon Journal installed, a dungeon's map has |cff6e2c0aOpen in Dungeon Journal|r on its Bosses tab, and clicking an entrance can open its page there instead of its map (the menu's |cff6e2c0aEntrances open Dungeon Journal|r, or Options). Its map still opens where Dungeon Journal has no page for it.",
		"|cff6e2c0aDungeon quests without Questie|r: the Quests tab works with Dungeon Journal or NeedRoll too, as a button that opens the dungeon's quests in it. With more than one installed, Options' |cff6e2c0aDungeon quests from|r picks which (the first installed: Questie, then Dungeon Journal, then NeedRoll).",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe OpenMap button off the map, if you like|r: |cff6e2c0aOpenMap button on the map|r (the menu's Look tab) hides it and the favourites. The menu is still a click away: OpenMap is in the minimap's AddOns list, and there's a |cff6e2c0aminimap button|r if you want one (the Look tab, or Options). Click for the map and its menu, right-click for the options window, drag it round the minimap; /openmap works too.",
		"|cff6e2c0aA choice the first time the map opens|r on a new install: |cff6e2c0aClassic|r (unexplored areas hidden, no dungeon or flight master icons, no zone levels, the favourite buttons folded away) or |cff6e2c0aOpenMap|r (as it comes). Settings you already have aren't asked about or changed; /openmap welcome asks again. Suggested in #24.",
		"|cff6e2c0aYour arrow on top, or off|r: the player arrow is drawn over every other icon on the map (quest givers, Questie's and other addons' icons), so you can always see which way you're facing (suggested in #31); your party's markers come up with it. Or take it off the world map (the menu's Show tab, |cff6e2c0aYour arrow|r) and find your way old-school by the land around you: your party still shows, and so does the minimap.",
		"|cff6e2c0aIcons from zoom|r: a slider (the menu's Look tab, or Options) for the zoom the icons for places (dungeons, boats, zeppelins and flight masters) show from: 1x has them from the whole world, higher keeps the map clean further out. Auto, as before, brings each in at its own zoom. Townsfolk never come in further out than their own; your pins, drawings and party always show.",
		"OpenMap shows under a |cff6e2c0aMap|r category in the game's AddOns list.",
		"|cff6e2c0aMap frame rate cap|r (the menu's Look tab, or Options; off unless you set it): the frame rate at most while the map is open. A big map draws many layers over the whole screen every frame; at 60 the graphics card does about half the work it does at 120 (reported: a full-screen 4K map doubling the card's power). Your own frame rate setting comes back as the map closes.",
		"Up close, a layer of the paper grain that has faded out is no longer drawn.",
		"|cff6e2c0aReport a problem|r sends you to OpenMap's comments on CurseForge for now, to post its code in (What's new's link goes to OpenMap's CurseForge page too). Its window, and the bench's and the map notes' to copy from, are in the map window's own frame.",
		"|cff6e2c0aDungeons, boats and zeppelins each have their own switch|r in the menu's Show tab and in Options, so you can keep dungeon and raid entrances and hide the boats or zeppelins. A kind that's off takes its routes with it when routes are shown. Your old setting carries over to all three.",
		"|cff6e2c0aOut of a city to its zone|r: right-click out of Stormwind, Ironforge, Darnassus, Orgrimmar, Thunder Bluff or Undercity and the map goes out to the zone around it (Elwynn Forest, Dun Morogh ...), as it does from anywhere else in that zone, not the whole continent.",
		"|cff6e2c0aAzeroth Tripview|r: its live ships and docks are kept above the map's art. For other addons, OpenMapAPI (version 2) can now place a point of the game's world anywhere on the stitched map, for frames they put on the world map themselves (docs/api.md).",
		"Zooming in quickly, the zones no longer flicker to blank parchment for a moment: the map's pre-drawn tiles now stay until every zone coming into view has its art in.",
		"Opening a dungeon's map no longer can raise a Lua error the first time (when the map window changed size as it opened, as in full screen).",
		"|cff6e2c0aWith a gamepad|r: the cursor stays where you put it. It jumped back to the middle of the map each time the map underneath changed (shortly after every zoom or pan), so the next zoom was about the middle. And in combat, a dungeon's or Zephras Isle's map waits until you're out of it (a line in chat says so): opened then, the game set the map's gamepad buttons again in a way it blocks in combat, which could leave them wrong until a /reload.",
		"|cff6e2c0aWoW Forever's boats|r are on the map, with their docks and routes: Steamwheedle Port (Tanaris) to Powderfuse Port (Riverglades), for both factions; Stormwind to Auberdine; and Menethil Harbor to Southshore and Auberdine, which takes the place of the old Menethil to Auberdine boat.",
		"|cff6e2c0aWoW Forever's flight masters|r: Farholde Keep and Powderfuse Port for the Alliance, Rog'mar and Powderfuse Port for the Horde, with their flights (Farholde Keep to Powderfuse Port, Lakeshire, Morgan's Vigil and Thelsamar; Rog'mar to Stonard, Kargath, Flame Crest and Hammerfall). The flight network now comes from WoW Forever's own tables, which have moved Stormwind's flight master and redrawn some of the classic flights.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe close-up minimap on towns by the sea and on islands|r: Menethil Harbor, Southshore, Theramore, Booty Bay's shallows, Teldrassil and Darnassus, Feathermoon Stronghold. It was cut to the continent map's coarse outline of the land, which leaves out what that map draws as sea; it now takes in each zone map's own land too.",
		"|cff6e2c0aNo retail Eversong Woods or Zul'Aman over Quel'Thalas|r: the minimap is now only the tiles the game itself draws (those its own world map file lists), which also leaves out other versions' sea far west of Dun Morogh and east of Wetlands, and the Draenei isles off Kalimdor.",
		"Blizzard's classic maps drawn in the land between zones are placed where WoW Forever places those zones. They were placed by Mists of Pandaria Classic's tables, whose zones are Cataclysm's, so The Barrens' was drawn at Northern Barrens' size and Stonetalon Mountains', Silithus', Badlands', Dun Morogh's and Azshara's were off, showing copies of their mountains beside the real ones. Cataclysm's Hillsbrad Foothills (Alterac taken in) and a different drawing of Mulgore are no longer used.",
		"The cave maps of four places WoW Forever doesn't have are gone: Greymane Manor (Gilneas), Spitescale Cavern (the Echo Isles as Cataclysm remade them), and Legion's Keeper's Rest and Karazhan Catacombs.",
		"|cff6e2c0aBooks on Map Forever|r's book icons show on the stitched map: they were drawn under its art. Which ones show is still the addon's own choice (those of the zone or continent the map is on).",
		"The zone you're looking at has its name over the map again when you hover it, where the game names no place in it (Silverpine Forest's had gone; reported in #25). With Zone levels off, zone names still show, without their levels.",
		"|cff6e2c0aMove Any|r owns the map window: with it, OpenMap's title bar, resize grips and saved place stand down, so Move Any's own drag and resize work on the map again (reported in #23). The map size slider and Reset size and place are off then.",
		"A city's own map that went missing (Ironforge showing only Dun Morogh's painting of it, until a /reload: reported in #30) is shown again when you reopen the map, and the map's check of what's in view no longer stays stuck if it stopped part way. (A safeguard: what hid it isn't known yet.)",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.4.0-beta", date = "2026-10-16", heads = { [1] = "New", [11] = "Improved", [20] = "Fixed", }, items = {
		"|cff6e2c0aDungeon maps.|r Click a dungeon's entrance for its own map, drawn from the game's own art (WoW Forever's map never shows it), right in the map window. Zoom with the wheel, drag to pan, and step through its floors with the arrows, the floor list or the side panel's Floors tab, which shows each floor as a small picture. Where several share an entrance you pick one; Blackrock Spire, Dire Maul and Scarlet Monastery are listed by wing, each opening on its own floor. Right-click, Escape or Back takes you back to the world where you were. 25 dungeons and raids have maps; WoW Forever's own new dungeons open on a blank page until the game has art for them.",
		"|cff6e2c0aA side panel for each dungeon|r, in the quest log's place and look, as a tab beside the log: its floors, its bosses, its quests (with Questie: their level, done or in your log, objectives on hover) and its loot, where we recommend NeedRoll by mikebvs (a boss's row opens it). Put the quest log away and the dungeon's map has the whole view; the tabs at the map's edge bring the log back.",
		"|cff6e2c0aDungeon entrances|r show their level range, coloured for your level (the menu's Level ranges hides them). WoW Forever's own dungeons are on the map: City of Dalaran, The Drowned City, Excavation Site: Wetlands, The Hall of Thanes and Ruins of Lordaeron so far.",
		"|cff6e2c0aMap pins|r, as many as you like: Ctrl-click the map (or Drop a pin) for one with a note and a colour. Its card follows it (Blizzard's waypoint, and TomTom's), shares it with your group, guild or a friend (other OpenMap players are asked first), gives a code to paste anywhere, or deletes it. The Pins list (/openmap pins) has them all, for all your characters.",
		"|cff6e2c0aThe quill:|r draw on the map with a pen, lines, arrows, circles and raid marks, in six inks and three widths (the menu's Quill, or /openmap draw). Your drawings are kept, and a pin's card can draw on that pin.",
		"|cff6e2c0aTabs at the map's edge|r for the OpenMap button and your favourites, in WoW Forever's own tab art. Drag the OpenMap tab anywhere round the edge; the arrow by it folds your favourites away. \"Buttons as edge tabs\" (the menu's Look tab) puts them back in the corner.",
		"|cff6e2c0aReport a problem draws:|r in two steps, draw where it's wrong (with the quill, or on a dungeon's page), then say what's wrong, for a code to paste into a GitHub issue.",
		"|cff6e2c0aWhen reopening the map:|r center on the player (the default for new installs), always restore the previous view, or restore it only while you're still in view. Middle-click the map to center on yourself at the same zoom. Thanks, C-Clymer (#19)!",
		"|cff6e2c0aWhat's new|r in the game, laid out like the quest log: each version's changes, Newer and Older, and where to find OpenMap on GitHub.",
		"|cff6e2c0aFor addon authors:|r OpenMapAPI (docs/api.md), to place things on the stitched world, hear when the view moves or a dungeon's map opens, and add a switch to the OpenMap menu or a section to a dungeon's panel.",
		"One place for OpenMap's settings: /openmap (and the game's AddOns settings page) opens the map's own menu, now with every setting in three tabs (On the map, Look, More) in the game's own settings look. The Look tab's sliders sit in two columns, with Defaults and Reset size and place under them.",
		"Other addons' map icons placed through HereBeDragons (TomTom, gatherers, notes addons) show on the stitched map from every zone in view, and Leatrix Maps' icons show above its art.",
		"Teldrassil's coast is whole, the great tree's roots all round the island, and Thunder Bluff comes in sooner, cut to its plan, under Mulgore's banner for it. (Changed textures: restart the game.)",
		"Darkened unexplored areas reach all of a zone's land and fade softly at their edges, with no hard lines or boxes in zones you've been to; cities you haven't found are darkened (or hidden) too. (Changed textures: restart the game.)",
		"The minimap's detail comes in after the same turns of the wheel in any window, full screen too, and a tall or very wide window brings the zones in by how much of the world is in view.",
		"The map pin's card, the pins list, What's new and the menu's dropdowns have the game's own frames and dropdown look; the coordinates are steady black boxes in the bottom-right corner; Find me has a crosshair; tooltips say plainly what a click does.",
		"The quest log's Back (from a quest's details) leaves the map where you're looking. The OpenMap menu shows over the quest log and stays put while you drag the map window, and the window's bottom-right corner is easier to grab with the quest log open.",
		"\"Reset sliders to defaults\" in Options, and Defaults under the menu's sliders.",
		"OpenMap gives back the game settings it holds: turn off its coordinates and Blizzard's come back, and at logout the map fade and coordinates are the game's own again.",
		"No more \"action blocked\" errors opening the map (or the quest log updating it) in combat (reported by C-Clymer in #19).",
		"Clicking a quest on another continent opens it at the first click.",
		"Zooming in on a zone no longer flashes plain parchment between its art from afar and close in.",
		"The quest log's button stays over the map's parchment border when you zoom right out, and its arrows point the way the log goes.",
		"A click on the window's resize corner without dragging no longer resets the view.",
		"Closing the map in the middle of resizing or moving it no longer leaves the window following the mouse.",
		"The menu's tabs no longer show another tab's names behind their own, and its search results aren't see-through.",
		"Clearing or replacing a map pin removes its TomTom waypoint.",
		"A flight route to or from a flight master you haven't learned says so.",
	} },
	{ version = "v0.3.0-beta", date = "2026-10-14", heads = { }, items = {
		"\"Minimap detail from\" (a slider in the menu, under Deepest zoom, and in Options' Up close) sets how far in the minimap's detail starts to mix in: lower comes in sooner, higher later (20x by default); at 1x it's there from the whole world. Further out than the game's own minimap tiles can be drawn, smaller copies of them show, crossfading to the tiles as you zoom in. (New textures: restart the game.)",
		"\"Minimap opacity\" (in the menu too, and Options' \"Minimap detail, most opacity\"): the most the minimap's detail ever shows, at any zoom.",
		"More coastal and border detail: each zone map now shows everything it paints round its own land (the sea off its coasts with its shallows, hatching and islets, the mountains and coasts beyond its border), shared out with its neighbours so each place shows one painting, handing over smoothly at the maps' frames. Land no map paints is plain parchment, which the art fades into, instead of the neighbours' edges blurred across it. The zone maps' sea names, their names for the neighbouring zones and their compass roses are left out. (Changed textures: restart the game.)",
		"Improved compatibility with other map addons: they work alongside OpenMap instead of fighting it. On the stitched map the art and the view are OpenMap's, and the rest of theirs keeps working; their map art shows on dungeon maps as before. At login OpenMap names only the options that still clash, not the whole addon.",
		"Gamepad: on the stitched map the right stick zooms at a steady pace all the way in and out (it crawled zoomed in), about the gamepad's cursor; A zooms into the zone under the cursor and X out a map, as clicks do, instead of changing the map underneath; the coordinates, the hover label, the zone highlight and the boat routes follow the gamepad's cursor. Its cursor shows the tooltips of OpenMap's buttons and map icons, and A presses them: the OpenMap button, the favourites, the menu (a slider goes to the value under the cursor), the dungeon, flight and other icons.",
		"\"Fade unexplored areas\" is now \"Darken unexplored areas\": the land you haven't explored is much darker and greyer, instead of faded toward the parchment, and a zone you haven't found at all is darkened whole from every zoom, the whole world's too, with the mountains and land round it, so a stretch you haven't been to is dark from one zone to the next. Only land is darkened, not the sea the zone maps paint round their coasts. (New textures: restart the game.)",
		"Panning and zooming make far less Lua garbage (OpenMap's view and zoom updates reuse their tables instead of making new ones every frame), so the game has less to clear up as you use the map.",
		"Clicking a quest in the quest log that's in another zone opens it again: the map goes to the quest's zone and stays there. It flickered and went back to the list, because the map was put back where you'd last closed it. Reopening where you left off now only applies when you open the map, not when Blizzard changes the map while it's open (the quest log, the zone dropdown), and not when the map opens on a quest's zone from the quest tracker.",
		"A quest's details in the quest log reach the foot of a window taller than Blizzard's, with more room for the quest's text, instead of stopping short with an empty strip under the buttons.",
		"The OpenMap button is its icon alone, right in the map's bottom-left corner.",
		"Zoomed in, only the tiles of each zone near the view are drawn and loaded, not every tile of every zone it touches, and panning works out what to show only now and then instead of every frame (the sea and the paper grain stay put as you pan, too). Less for the game to draw and lay out as you move about.",
		"The zones' art is baked into world tiles (made by a script from Blizzard's map art, as the map draws it), so from the continents' zoom in to a zone the map draws a few dozen tiles instead of hundreds of masked textures; closer in than the tiles' own pixels, the zones' art is drawn live as before. Changing the colour match, or hiding unexplored areas, uses the live art throughout. (New textures, 69 MB: restart the game.)",
		"The continents' and seas' names cost far less to pan and zoom: only those near the view are drawn, and their halo takes half as many font strings (each copy's shadow is the one opposite it), the same to look at. Panning over a continent with its names showing was a third of the map's frame time on a wide screen. While the map moves (zooming or panning) their halo rests (every letter is drawn again at its new size on each frame of a zoom, and laid out again on each of a pan, and the halo was eight of its nine), back as soon as the map stops.",
		"Questie's icons from the neighbouring zones are placed up to half the map's width round it, not a whole width: every icon on the map is laid out again on each frame of a pan or zoom (231 of them cost 7 ms a frame on a wide screen). Those further off show once the map switches to their zone.",
		"Panning and zooming no longer lay out the thousands of zone textures that aren't showing (the live art the baked tiles stand in for, the tiles off the view): a hidden one lets go of its place on the map until it shows again. With vsync off on a wide screen, all of OpenMap's art cost 20 ms of a 41 ms panning frame, 8 of them in art nobody could see.",
		"Up close over Orgrimmar the minimap's detail is much fainter (15% at most, from 50%): the city's own plan, which comes in from further out than the other cities', leads there.",
		"OpenMap's icons (flight masters, dungeons, the player arrow ...) are on the map's view instead of its canvas: they keep their size on screen by themselves, instead of their layer being rescaled on every frame of a zoom (which laid every icon out again: 6.6 ms of a zooming frame).",
		"/openmap bench times the map where it's slow (still, panning and zooming, at several zooms, then with each part of it off in turn) and gives the results to copy into an issue.",
		"The OpenMap menu's close button is easier to hit, and Escape closes the menu.",
		"\"Report a problem\" isn't only about the map: circling a spot is optional (just click Next), it works on dungeon maps too, and the issue form says so.",
		"The debug overlay also shows what can pile up over a session: the UI's Lua memory and how fast it grows, the map's pins (every addon's, and the kind there's most of), how much zone art is loaded, how many regions are placed live, which parts make the most Lua garbage a second (rescaling every addon's pins, switching maps, OpenMap's own updates), and which addons hold the most memory and grow it fastest.",
	} },
}
